<http://data.silknow.org/object/94d09ae9-6ef9-3985-997b-455327eff9c2>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Bertha collar of blonde needle lace and silk ribbon, Ireland, 1825-1850"@en , "Bertha collar of blonde needle lace and silk ribbon. Open in the front and made of a series of borders of white silk bobbin lace patterned with trefoil leaves and formal ornament, and mounted in two curves on a ground of machine-made net. The collar is decorated with three bows and a narrow band near the top edge of yellow silk ribbon woven with a design of cone-shapes and curving lines of strapwork."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5338e66c-98ae-3d7b-926f-7963671414a0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Bertha collar of blonde needle lace and silk ribbon, Ireland, 1825-1850"@en , "Bertha collar of blonde needle lace and silk ribbon. Open in the front and made of a series of borders of white silk bobbin lace patterned with trefoil leaves and formal ornament, and mounted in two curves on a ground of machine-made net. The collar is decorated with three bows and a narrow band near the top edge of yellow silk ribbon woven with a design of cone-shapes and curving lines of strapwork."@en ;
